  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>KP</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;represents Freundlich adsorption isotherm. It is an empirical relationship between the amount of gas adsorbed by a given amount of solid adsorbent surface and pressure of the gas at a particular temperature.</p><p>So, Freundlich adsorption isotherm equation is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>KP</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>logK</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mfrac><mi>logP</mi></math></p><p>Extent of adsorption&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math>&nbsp;decreases with increase in temperature.</p><p>With the help of the above two equation, following plots are obtained</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7ce9c9db-d3dc-43ee-9116-350e911e95d7.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 195px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6dfb9cd5-1282-45a2-849d-38f839b0aa46.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 166px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5097b1b8-eb8f-4346-98b9-d81285774e92.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 196px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>",
